</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 13, 2005 - 6:41 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Embersage! <BR> <BR>me again :-&#41; still unregistered :-&#40; <BR> <BR>  I was trying to figure out the meaning of the shoe pyramid in Mrs Davis&#39; house when I came across this site and found this report. &#40;I hope AOL doesn&#39;t mess up the chart&#41;  <BR> <BR>Don&#39;t know if anyone came across this report and posted it.  <BR>I recall reading that there was a plane crash a few days before the Otero killings.  <BR>January 12, 1974 is also the same day Michael Williams &#40;Coleman&#41; was shot after opening the door and then closing it in the face of two assaillants. It would be interesting to find out what time it happened. Is the crash and shooting related. <BR> <BR>I wonder if this is that plane crash report. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.ntsb.gov/ntsb/brief.asp?ev_id=83667&amp;key=0" target=_top>http://www.ntsb.gov/ntsb/brief.asp?ev_id=83667&amp;key =0</a> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>NTSB Identification: MKC74FCQ22 <BR>14 CFR Part 91 General Aviation  <BR>Event occurred Saturday, January 12, 1974 in WICHITA, KS <BR>Aircraft: PIPER PA-31P, registration: N33CG <BR>-------------------------------------------------- -------------------------------------------------- ------------------------ <BR> FILE    DATE          LOCATION          AIRCRAFT DATA       INJURIES       FLIGHT                        PILOT DATA <BR>                                                               F  S M/N     PURPOSE <BR>-------------------------------------------------- -------------------------------------------------- ------------------------ <BR>3-0074  74/1/12    WICHITA,KANS        PIPER PA-31P        CR-  0  0  1  NONCOMMERCIAL             AIRLINE TRANSPORT, AGE <BR>        TIME - 1220                    N33CG               PX-  0  0  1  BUSINESS                  48, 3681 TOTAL HOURS, 123 <BR>                                       DAMAGE-SUBSTANTIAL  OT-  0  0  0                            IN TYPE, INSTRUMENT <BR>                                                                                                   RATED. <BR>        NAME OF AIRPORT - PIPER <BR>        DEPARTURE POINT             INTENDED DESTINATION <BR>          SALT LAKE CITY,UTAH         WICHITA,KANS <BR>        TYPE OF ACCIDENT                                         PHASE OF OPERATION <BR>           GEAR COLLAPSED                                           LANDING: ROLL <BR>        PROBABLE CAUSE&#40;S&#41; <BR>           PILOT IN COMMAND - FAILED TO FOLLOW APPROVED PROCEDURES,DIRECTIVES,ETC. <BR>           MISCELLANEOUS ACTS,CONDITIONS - NOT ALIGNED WITH RUNWAY/INTENDED LANDING AREA <BR>        FACTOR&#40;S&#41; <BR>           AIRPORTS/AIRWAYS/FACILITIES - AIRPORT CONDITIONS: OTHER <BR>           MISCELLANEOUS ACTS,CONDITIONS - OVERLOAD FAILURE <BR>        REMARKS- LNDD IN DRIFTED SNOW ADJ TO RWY.PLT RECOGNIZED ERROR TOO LATE TO MAKE A GO-AROUND. <BR> <BR>Index for Jan1974 | Index of months   <BR> <BR> <BR>Also, do you have any knowledge if anyone in Mrs Davis&#39; family was in service? Gulf war? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
