</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 15, 2005 - 11:06 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->But whats important...where did the record of the plane wreck come from and can we use the same source to find the crash of at plane wreck in miami jan 14 1974 departed puerto rico bound for wichita. to carry a ton and a half&#40;3000#&#41; of pot, it would have to be a twin engine or a modified wwII single engine bomber&#40; I&#39;d look for an old Twin engine Beech, piper, cessna, or vinage dcxx transport&#41; Of coarse it did crash so it may had been a large single that was overloaded.If we could run down the pilot, who if not killed was probably arrested, then we might find a link to Otero &#40; the cops have checked, but if it linked williams into the deal, thats been hushed&#41; and when the cops were checking ,they didn&#39;t have a name on Rader. and I doubt any of the new guys have paid attention to that. <BR> <BR>But the best I can remember, the price of pot around that time was skyrocketing from around $140 a pound up to around $800 in the span of around two years. so the plane was carrying around $150000 worth of merchandise. <BR> <BR>If it was being brought in by an organized smuggling operation, it was probably written off as the cost of doing business. But that was back when it was still conceivable for an amature who didn&#39;t mind taking chances to do &#34;one big run&#34;and scratch $150000 together and buy pot in mexico or columbia or whatever &#40;without having to deal with scary people like a cartel or crime lord&#41; smuggle it in and double their money. But the money was paid up front. If this was the case, somebody or a lot of somebodies were out their life savings and there should have been, at the very least a rash of divorces, and probably some extra crime by those trying to recoup their cash or who were just pissed off. <BR> <BR>If, by chance, the plane was local and aged, that would point to a small run. Big time crooks would use good equiptment to ensure they didn&#39;t get busted. Small timers were just counting on luck, after all , it only had to work once.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
