<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11902"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, March 20, 2005 - 6:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree with Tac, and as i have said before, I never really paid that much attention to this crash before, when Otero&#39;s died, but there is so much now that makes this crash important, I think some how it ties into the 3 dudes, Lewis and Rader I just can&#39;t put my finger on it, but all the guys that got laid off went to work at colemans, it adds up somehow<!--/Text--></td></tr>
