<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12066"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, March 22, 2005 - 6:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B, <BR> <BR>In BTK Communications section under &#34;Christ on Cross: Alpha &amp; Omega&#34;  a post by Itty dated March 22nd states that NewMexican stated that BTK worked on hydraullics while in the Airforce. Was Rader part of a flight crew or maintenance for fighters ?  <BR> <BR>If so then Rader could have easily been recruited by smugglers to do flight checks. Just as easily he could have sabotaged any flight check.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
