<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12289"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 26, 2005 - 4:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E, <BR> <BR>Allen Long was one of the first major Pot Smugglers in America. He has a book out called &#34;Smoke Screen&#34; in paperback and in hard cover it goes by &#34;Loaded&#34; with author Robert Sabbag.  <BR> <BR>At the end of this book in 1978-1979 time frame Long describes his life in Miami. Long move to Miami due to a serious connection. The connection Long made was with a group of smugglers who were according to Long from LE backgrounds. <BR> <BR>This group had a few Miami cops and &#34;agency&#34; members. They were able to smuggler 100s of tons of Pot into Florida with complete ammunity to prosecution.  .  .   <BR> <BR>If Otero was part of a govt. covert smuggling operation it would not surprise me. Long&#39;s book states that he stopped the actual smuggling part of his operation because his new partners would never get busted.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Govt drug dealing is a reality as we have seen with many journalists chronicling the cocaine conspiracy&#39;s involving the CIA.  .  .   <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
