</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 26, 2005 - 11:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Absolutely right. Plus the fact that there is no evidence of the names of the 3 killed in the crash, plus the rumors which circulated right after the Otero murders, plus the reluctance of the police to release details of the Otero crime scene which was originally described as &#34;execution style&#34;, keeps directing my instincts to think there was more than routine ciminal activity afoot. If thats not enough in the &#34;inside the BTK file&#34; posting under news on the home page or: <BR> <BR> &#40;click this link&#41; <a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/inside.html" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/inside.html</a> <BR> <BR> <BR>Read, under the red heading &#39;BTK suspects&#39; about the guy with the blue car and blue pickup. It doesn&#39;t mention which shade of blue, but the Military Police at McConnell Air Force Base, and the Troops which made the rounds to all of the missile bases drove dark blue cars or pickup trucks. &#40;bet everyone forgot about Debbie...I wonder if there are any tracks left from that wreck at Greenwich and Kellog?&#41; <BR> <BR>All of this smuggling stuff has probably been covered up from the BTK angle, however the point of the CIA being involved in the first place is all tied into the Iran/Contra affair. Ergo I am going to shake that tree and see what falls out since some of that stuff has been recently declassified. For that matter, that could have been what Otero was involved with in the first place &#40;who knows, they may have needed radio antennas too&#41;. <BR> <BR>Don&#39;t give up on the smugglers though, and remember that they WERE smuggling pot so their memories may not be to great. Any wreck &#40;preferably airplane&#41; in the general Gulf of Mexico/Carribean/Atlantic Ocean area &#40;preferrably Florida&#41; around the 70&#39;s &#40;preferrably January 1974&#41; is of interest...surely they would remember,at least,that much.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
