<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12420"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 30, 2005 - 9:57 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->ok Tac here&#39;s my thought then, why would these three men that died in this crash not be named, we all know it wasn&#39;t really a big deal, becuase everyone was doing it back then, so why not give us the names of these three guys in this crash. What was the big secret. Th press talked about the crash but never say who was on that plane<!--/Text--></td></tr>
