<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12435"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 30, 2005 - 3:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E, <BR> <BR>In 1974 not everyone was doing it. This was the beginning stages of pot flights into Florida. In addition the snow blind blizzard of Lehder and Jung had not changed American culture yet. America was still a pot smoking country.  .  . coke did not take over until a few years later and with coke came the media attention. <BR> <BR>IMO it was not a shipment big enough to be a covert govt operation. IMO &#40;it is a total guess&#41; one of the 3 pilots was either a son or relative to a politician or important public figure with political ties.  <BR> <BR>Because the time frame is the beginning of these smuggling flights the public and media would find this crash to be a big news worthy event ! <BR> <BR>The big secret was that someone of recognition was part of that flight. That someone if recognized would have tied someone powerful to the attempt to smuggle pot into the US.  .  .  just a theory. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
