<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12436"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 30, 2005 - 4:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->E, <BR> <BR>one other thought.  .  . if I am not mistaken Geradine Ferraro, during her push for pres nomination, had dirt dug up on her husband&#39;s dealings with underworld. In addition wasn&#39;t her son also investigated and found to be dealing blow out of his college campus dorm ?  <BR> <BR>If I have the facts right then let me tie it into my previous post. Public perception is everything whether the media has the facts right or wrong. <BR> <BR>In Ferraro&#39;s case very powerful people did NOT want a woman president and made sure to find the &#34;goods&#34; on her. <BR> <BR>IMO the plane crash holds the same type of &#34;goods&#34; on somebody of conscequence.  <BR> <BR>It would be very very interesting to know if any politician of power or CIA type agency head of power lost a son in 1974 ???????????????? <BR> <BR>The other possible wild card in this is if one of the 3 was a foriegn diplomat&#39;s son or a son of a foriegn person of power ????????<!--/Text--></td></tr>
