<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12468"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 31, 2005 - 3:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Otero was stationed at Albrook AFB which was the ORIGINAL International Air Force Base, which is the airborne sibling of The School Of The Americas, which also was origially in Panama. <BR> <BR><a href="http://zmagsite.zmag.org/Jan2004/wray0104.html" target=_top>http://zmagsite.zmag.org/Jan2004/wray0104.html</a> <BR> <BR>According to Beattie&#39;s book, Otero was also the personal mechanic for the Torrijos &#40;defacto leader of Panama at the time&#41;. Also , at that time, Manuel Noriega was acting chief of Military Intelligence. For those of you too young to remember, the U.S. later lauched an actual military invasion into Panama to &#34;arrest&#34; and &#34;extradite&#34; Noriega who &#40;I think&#41; eventually gained contol of the country, and is currently a &#34;prisoner of war&#34; in the U.S. being held for smuggling drugs [by plane] to the U.S. <BR> <BR>It is pretty easy to imagine that Otero&#39;s and Noriega&#39;s paths had crossed somewhere along the line, &#40;particularly considering the fact that the book points out that in Panama Otero was living a &#34;double life&#34; keeping both a mistress and a family, and told his family &#40;whether or not it was true, or a cover for his philandering&#41; that he was working for the CIA.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
