<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12485"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 31, 2005 - 12:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B, <BR> <BR>That is huge news to me !  As you well know Noriega granted assylum to Escobar &amp; patriots in the cartel in the late 80&#39;s. He also was being paid huge cash to act as a fueling stop for shipments. <BR> <BR>Back in 1974, if Otero was dirty, he would have most likely been a pot smuggler and not coke. With this in mind, Otero may have a connection to the same supply of drugs as Allen Long and George Jung: Columbia.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Columbian pot was the best in the world at that time especially the Santa Marta &#34;Gold&#34; variety. If Otero and the plane crash are connected it may be very likely that Long &amp; friends may know the guys that crashed.  <BR> <BR>Long is about to have a movie made of his life based on the book Smoke Screen.  .  .  the answer to the crash victim identification most likely lays with him.  .  . <!--/Text--></td></tr>
