<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12541"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 3:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B, <BR> <BR>Point well taken. If Otero was &#34;company&#34; we can forget about finding anything the easy way through research.  <BR> <BR>I highly doubt that there is any time capsuled information about to be released on this incident.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Frankly the only hope,imo, of finding out the names of our smugglers is through another smuggler from that era.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
