<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12542"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 3:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->One last very alarming thought.  .  . I have read internet articles, by googling Carlos Lehder, written by a rogue journalist who claims that Lehder has never spent a day in prison after his life sentence for trafficing.  <BR> <BR>Why ? According to the article, Lehder is working for the US Govt has their liason in S.America for the express purpose of bringing coke into this country. Lehder is dealing drugs for the CIA.  .  .  <BR> <BR>The journalist claimed to have tracked Lehder down to a suburb outside of San Francisco.  .  . Lafayette, CA. He claims that Lehder was LISTED in the 411 directory. <BR> <BR>The most amazing claim was that Lehder&#39;s wife was a high ranking official, with no discernable capacity, for the insurance giant AIG in San Francisco.  .  .   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
