</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 01, 2005 - 5:39 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tac <BR> <BR>I&#39;m also thinking that the only way to find the names would be a lucky hit in the obits &#40;and subsequently tie them in using the name[s] by cross-referencing&#41; or by finding them in an anectdote told by a fellow smuggler or law enforcement member. Someone in the WPD knows them though, you can bet on that.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
