<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12572"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 12:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Meanwhile...back at the plane crash: <BR> <BR>Page 31 &#40;NIW&#41; RE: The plane crash <BR> <BR>Chief Floyd: &#34;There is nothing to show that the family was involved in illicit activity of any kind&#34;. <BR> <BR>Whereas Bob Beattie adds: &#34;But privately, they still believed it was a strong lead&#34;. &#40;And I assume he has reason to feel that they did [and seeing that he is a lawyer, is confident that he could back it up if need be]&#41;. <BR> <BR>Page 32 &#40;NIW&#41; [ Panamanian military police are called &#34;Dennys&#34;] <BR> <BR>Page 33 &#40;NIW&#41; &#34;The policemen discovered that Joseph Otero had &#34;monetary conflicts&#34; with five persons [dude] in Panama. The conflicts were over business deals involving flying merchandise into Panama from South America. All five [dude] were in the United States and were being searched for by the Wichita police. Two of them [dude] had already been interviewed, one in Wichita and another in New Mexico. With the new information about the business deals, however, both of those individuals [dude] were reinterviewed&#34;. <BR> <BR>There is no mention about whether the other three individuals [dude] were ever located. So... we have with 5 dude to start with, 2 dude were accounted for. That means we are still missing &#34;three dude&#34;. <BR> <BR>Could it be possible that they had, maybe engine trouble on their way to the United States...?  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12572-->
<!--Post: 12574--><!--Time: 1112483802-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12574"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 3:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B, <BR> <BR>Geez this is getting convoluted, interesting, and frustrating all rolled into one mess.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Much agreed on your assessment to our probability of gaining information. IMO obits would have been deleted or never reported if these names were somehow &#34;black listed&#34; by the CIA.  .  .   <BR> <BR>The 2 &#34;dudes&#34; that are accounted for do we have names for them ?  <BR> <BR>I also agree that either a past or current detective in the WPD has knowledge of the smuggler&#39;s identity.  .  . but here is the problem.  .  .   <BR> <BR>In Allen Long&#39;s last smuggling group he worked with men who were CIA &amp; local Miami Dade cops.  .  .  One afternoon in a meeting, Long&#39;s partners introduced him to a Sheriff of a small town in Georgia. Apparently this Sheriff was corrupt and part of the conspiracy to hide incoming flights into the Georgia backwoods.  .  .   <BR> <BR>My point is that it is very believable to me that someone on the WPD may have been involved in this smuggling operation as protection. If this is the case we can figure on NO help from LE.  .  .   <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12574-->
<!--Post: 12575--><!--Time: 1112484381-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12575"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 3:26 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B, <BR> <BR>I love your stuff keep sending info.  .  .  <BR> <BR>Here is a very long shot indeed but.  .  . how far is Chicago from Wichita ? The following man could very well provide our answers.  .  .   <BR> <BR>In the early 1970s Lee Carlyle was a major pot smuggler &#40;source Mexico&#41;. Lee was a distributor who sold off major weight to dealers around the midwest.  <BR> <BR>One of Carlyle&#39;s last loads into Chicago was to be smuggled via big rig truck out of Mexico up to Chicago.  .  . the load &amp; driver got busted right outside the boarder.  .  . someone dropped a dime. . . Carlyle left the midwest for Miami. <BR> <BR>The significance is that Carlyle was connected in our timeframe to Allen Long and the midwest pot scene.  .  .   <BR> <BR>The interesting possibility ?  Carlyle was busted for smuggling blow into FLA. According to &#34;Smoke Screen&#34; as of 2000 Lee Carlyle was serving a prison term for his last &#34;adventure.&#34;  <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t know if this is a Federal beef or State. Most likely Federal.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Do you think we could track this guy down ?  I wonder if he would agree to be interviewed ?  <BR> <BR>Btw I am currently in contact with a close friend of George Jung. This friend has asked questions of George for me. George answers some and leaves others alone.  .  .  I will see if I can get lucky. <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
