<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12583"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 5:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Florida seems to be the safe haven. Butterworth headed for Florida too. I&#39;m hoping that we are not getting into the business of the the guys with the big shoulders. The CIA is one thing, but when guys with no necks start showing up, I&#39;m outta here. <BR> <BR>Keep trying to make contact but walk softly. Make sure they understand that we are working this angle because we are interested in the Otero murders only &#40;out of curiosity, and not curiosity that is so stubborn that we are not responsive to verbal threats&#41;&#40;or at least warning shots&#41;. <BR> <BR>Chicago and Kansas City have always been somewhat tied together crimewise, they are the &#34;mid west&#34; Wichita is nowhere comparable in size to either &#40;especially when you combine KC KS &#43; KC MO&#41;. But if someone is driving from Texas to KC or Chicago the way to go would be I-35 through Wichita to KC then continue on to Chicago. <BR> <BR>Somewhere along the line I remember a Circle-K Transport that ran from Texas to Desmoines [dee-moyne, iowa], but I don&#39;t remember why it was brought up, and it would make more sense to be apportioned as an independent long hauler. <BR> <BR>If the &#34;three dude&#34; are tied to the &#34;five dude&#34; that Otero had financial problems with and if the &#34;five dude&#34; are tied to any of The CIA,DEA, The Association of Crooked Cops, The Guys with the Big Shoulders, Manuel Noriega, and I&#39;m beginning to suspect The Boy Scouts of America...It&#39;s pretty much ancient history now so keep plugging...&#40;after all they are writing books, it can&#39;t be all that secret anymore&#41;. <BR> <BR>Ember wants to keep on the &#34;symbol&#34; and Skov added more today...the notorious BTK symbol looks like every scribble ever made. The 2004 code is still there and may contain a clue...after all the plane wreck was the second thing to happen in 74. <BR> <BR>Also Beattie, when talking about Coleman, mentioned, out of the wild blue, that Coleman sometimes had huge government contracts [military] for some reason. Guess we are going to have to look at that. The military, particularly Air Force keeps popping up &#40;and New Mexico&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Also Beattie&#39;s book also points out that Otero WAS at one time stationed at McConnell[384 air wing or something]&#40;outfits that pop up for a year or two then dissolve, especially during peace time, are usually Special Ops&#41;. It might be that Rader and Otero did cross paths at McConnell. <BR> <BR>Plenty to work on...keep an eye peeled as you read Beattie&#39;s book. He mentions stuff offhand, but raising a question or pointing to something, throughout the book.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12583-->
<!--Post: 12584--><!--Time: 1112494897-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12584"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, April 02, 2005 - 6:21 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok since you want just put it all out there, lets go for it till someone shuts us up, Other writers have gone in this direction and stoped So I guess it will be up to those of us brave enough to search for the truth. I am concerned about new info such as the drawing of the pair of scissors stuck in the dolls head that Tom took off the beginning of the site, Sherry Baker had them in her head. We have to go back to the beginning, with the Otero&#39;s and the crash andColemans to figure out all the rest. While your at it read the Z files the similarites are amazing.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12584-->
<!--Post: 12852--><!--Time: 1113427669-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12852"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 13, 2005 - 2:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B &amp; Em <BR> <BR>I have attempted to pass forward questions to George Jung through a contact but I have never received confirmation or any other information.  <BR> <BR>Likewise the Lehder info trail goes cold with limited information.  .  .   <BR> <BR>I am reading the Beattie book and if it is believeable, aka Graysmith proof, there are many connections to the possibility that drugs were the linchpin to this case.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Where to look now seems like as big a mystery as the angle we are pursuing.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12852-->
<!--Post: 12855--><!--Time: 1113435989-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12855"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 13, 2005 - 4:46 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I was thinkin&#39;...haven&#39;t done anything about it yet...but I&#39;ve definately been thinkin&#39;, that rather than omitting the obituaries altogether, the date of death may have been altered. Instead of listing the death as occurring January 14, for instance, it might be misprinted January 10, or 16, or 9, etc.. <BR> <BR>Of course there is also the problem of: were they American, Puerto Rican, Mexican, or did the names they used even exist. They may have been buried in unmarked graves &#40;not knowing where to send them&#41;. <BR> <BR>I believe something, however led the WPD to think that the plane was enroute to Wichita from Puerto Rico. They must know something about the occupants, since there was no flight plan.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12855-->
<!--Post: 12860--><!--Time: 1113451929-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12860"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 13, 2005 - 9:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Good Points guys, and B, when we started looking for the three guys I was doing research on the obits. In Puerto Rico. I only looked a the 14th as well. So I will go back. There was a reason our cops went there and I think that is why. For anyone reading our ideas, If you can help, it would be great. Thanks Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
