<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12862"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 13, 2005 - 10:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Nobody else believes us Ember, they all think we are nuts...but we know we are okay...we are okay...we are okay...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12862-->
<!--Post: 12878--><!--Time: 1113522994-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12878"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jed4258<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jed4258<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 14, 2005 - 4:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule - In your post above you mentioned McConnell&#39;s 384th.  This wasn&#39;t a special ops wing or anything devious of any sort.  It was the 384th Air Refueling Wing, they flew the KC135A&#39;s and eventually the KC135R&#39;s.  This was a part of SAC &#40;Strategic Air Command&#41;. <BR> <BR>I was stationed with them in 81-84<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12878-->
<!--Post: 12879--><!--Time: 1113526762-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12879"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, April 14, 2005 - 5:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->B &amp; Em, <BR> <BR>Today a national news report hit the wires about the biggest Extacy drug bust in US History. The dealers it turned out were part of the US Air National guard and they transported the drugs on the Airforce&#39;s largest cargo airplane.  .  .   <BR> <BR>IMO this type of behavior has been going on since the early 1970s.  <BR> <BR>B I think you are correct that LE knew &#34;something&#34; about our mystery pilots but.  .  .   <BR> <BR>IMO if the drugs/plane was on route to land in Wichita it most likely would have done so without the drugs aboard the plane. <BR> <BR>In the early days of smuggling most planes either landed at makeshift hidden runways OR the bales were pushed out of the plane to be scooped up by a ground crew for delivery via truck.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Another possibility is that our &#34;boys&#34; were commissioned to &#34;carry&#34; a partial load for delivery to a Florida connection by flying low and pushing bales out of the plane over a designated drop zone.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12879-->
<!--Post: 12881--><!--Time: 1113550069-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12881"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 15, 2005 - 12:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yes, I like that Idea Tac, I think the problem, from the flight manifest was that the person flying, didn&#39;t know how to land. Maybe as we think, because he wasn&#39;t suppose to be the one flying the plane. Hey we left out the Coleman supervisior in our thinking. Wonder if the &#34;Robbery&#34; was pay back for the plane crash, since he may have backed out at the last min, too. Thank you Jed, with your experience we are counting on you now to help us keep the facts straight. And B, They know what we are talking about is true, but No one wants to admit it. LOL and I have been called a lot of odd things lately because of the 340 cipher, that just because no one in 30 years has been able to crack it, it must no be real or whatever. ThatI am wasting my time. Guess who cracked the 340. So If I am a nut, at least I, like you guys can think for myself out side the box, and thank God, cause if we didn&#39;t think this way nothing would ever be solved. Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12881-->
<!--Post: 12892--><!--Time: 1113591833-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12892"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 15, 2005 - 12:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The &#34;backdoor&#34; connection to all of this would be to find a ground crew member for this flight. If this flight was orchestrated by the govt or a police agency then the ground crew would also be LE.  .  .  <BR> <BR>But if the &#34;boys&#34; were freelancing without LE ties then the ground crew would be civilians. <BR> <BR>Ground crews usually consisted of offloaders and logistic/communication/spotters.  .  .  <BR> <BR>Allen Long&#39;s system of landing load included multiple drop/landing zones. In one instance they used Darlington Speedway two other covert landing zones.  <BR> <BR>The idea of the 3 possible landing zones is that the 3 separate logistic/spotters could survey ea landing site for possible LE surveilance. The plane would then be given the &#34;Ok&#34; for one of the 3 zones avoiding LE. <BR> <BR>In addition the multiple landing zone idea then keeps the ground crews in the dark. This could thwart a ground crew member from rolling over and ratting out the landing site to LE. Since none of the ground crews knew, when if ever, the plane would land security could be maintained.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12892-->
<!--Post: 12999--><!--Time: 1113930433-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST12999"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 10:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have an idea, who about we do try a &#34;Back door&#34; approach. Can we look up police busts in the news at that time, before and after this crash and see who was running drugs in and out of Wichita? Or who the major players in the drug market where?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 12999-->
