<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13002"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 12:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ember, what is the 340?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13002-->
<!--Post: 13014--><!--Time: 1113967685-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13014"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 8:28 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->In 1977 Vern Miller became DA.  He hired a young prosecutor from the KC area who was running a multi-layered drug task force to establish a similar task force with WPD, Sedg.Co. SO, and DEA.  The task force operated for four years doing nothing but drug prosecutions, and with a prosecutor who filed and prosecuted all drug cases from 1977 through 1980. <BR> <BR>As I happen to know the former prosecutor, I passed your question along. <BR> <BR>In 1975 or 1976 a dealer was busted at K-Mart in east Wichita with over 100 lbs of grass.  Exact amount was unknown.  The task force &#34;reverse engineered&#34; the supply chain and filed a conspiracy case, which included people very highly, connected to McConnell AFB. <BR> <BR>In 1974 or 1975 a plane similar to the Miami crash plane landed at a rural Sedgwick abandoned airfield to refuel.  It ran off the runway and got stuck in mud.  Local police found it partially unloaded. <BR> <BR>Kansas has lots of abandoned airfields, and at that time was a major clandestine re-fueling point for pot smugglers. <BR> <BR>Cocaine followed the mj but was not nearly as common as it is now.  The task force made a three-kilo bust in 1977; it was far and away the biggest in Wichita during that period. <BR> <BR>Heroin was mostly confined to northeast Wichita. <BR> <BR>From 1977 to 1978, most drug dealers were small local groups who had connections in Mexico or with other larger suppliers.  There were no real organized interstate operations like now.  Hell&#39;s Angels were the closest with organized traffic.  They bought guns with drug proceeds, smuggled them into Mexico and traded them for drugs. <BR> <BR>In 1979 we began seeing the emergence of Latin American gangs. &#34;Mexican Mafia” They were pushing local groups out and gaining control of the mj and coke supply side operations. <BR> <BR>Unfortunately the new DA, Clark Owens, in 1980 withdrew the assigned prosecutor and the intelligence network collapsed.  &#40;The DA&#39;s office no longer supported trading low-level sales cases for cases against higher-up suppliers.&#41; <BR> <BR>Eight years later, with a new DA, the office changed again, but there was no way to rebuild the infrastructure of informants.  The Latin organizations were firmly in control, and there was no intelligence on their structure.   <BR> <BR>Ember:  The drug operations in the early &#39;70s were very different.  Kansas was a major mj way station.  Pot sold for more, farther north, where it was too cold for it to grow naturally.  The connection in those years with significant Latin American operations would have mostly support for refueling.  Mechanical repair of the aircraft was also important because most of the aircraft were poorly maintained and equipped.  Crashes like the Miami event were common; most landings were at night on airfields lit by car headlights.  Crews were poorly trained and tired. <BR> <BR>I’ll be glad to pass on any more questions. <BR> <BR>Phoenix <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13014-->
<!--Post: 13028--><!--Time: 1113979957-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13028"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, April 19, 2005 - 11:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Phoenix, <BR> <BR>Excellent short history of the Wichita area&#39;s drug activity; I am happy to say that you bolstered my initial theories on Wichita. I figured that it was more &#34;weigh &amp; fuel&#34; than actual destination.  <BR> <BR>In books by Allen Long, George Jung, and Max Mermelstein Chicago was identified as a major area infested by their crews. <BR> <BR>In Long&#39;s book  one of his partners, Lee Carlyle, was a major player in Chi who brought in mj from Mexico via small aircraft and big rig.  <BR> <BR>The refueling stops were as you described hidden strips carved out of nature but concealed; most of the ground crews were &#34;family&#34; men trying to make extra cash. Sadly many got sucked in after getting a taste.  .  .   <BR> <BR>George Jung famous for Coke took his first big pinch in Chicago trying to unload hundreds of pounds of pot he drove into town via a Winnebago.  .  .  <BR> <BR>Due to the lack of information regarding the unidentified 3 pilots that crashed, do you think it possible to track down any ground crew or mechanic&#39;s attached to this flight ? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13028-->
<!--Post: 13033--><!--Time: 1113998914-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13033"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 5:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you Phoenix for the information, And Tac I think that is where we have to start, back into the reseach aspect. If you go to The news papers in Puerto Rico for that time, they will tell you every detail of everything going on. And there had to be a task force for this. Meaning that some of there minutes are published somewhere. Itty the 340 is a Zodiac Cipher. It is 340 symbols and letters that form a statement that no one has ever been able to decipher in 30 years. I was told when I was as to do it, that most people thought it was impossible to solve or that I would be called crazy for trying. My point in bringing it up here? Was that no idea or thought is crazy. That went people say there is nothing there, We need to look harder. Becuase someone is hiding something. The 340 was hard, but I stuck with it and now it is decoded. So I think somewhere, somehow we are going to find out that this plane crash has something to do with Joe Otero&#39;s death. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13033-->
<!--Post: 13034--><!--Time: 1113999436-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13034"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Phoenix<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Phoenix<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->3-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 5:17 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A lot of information on CIA drug activity in Central America in the &#39;70s and &#39;80s is surfacing now under the Freedom Of Information act.  I had a lot of it when I was researching School Of the Americas.  If I can find it, I&#39;ll post the links. If memory serves me correctly, Noriega had CIA backing in the beginning. <BR> <BR>Phoenix<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13034-->
<!--Post: 13056--><!--Time: 1114040116-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13056"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 4:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Noriega had backing in the beginning then the US nailed him for doing what he was doing before when he was in favor with our govt.  .  . acting as a safe haven for SAmerican drug lords &amp; a fueling stop for flights into the US.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Phoenix the more interesting and mind boggling task to tackle, and I invite you to try, is to dig up information on the whereabouts of Carlos Lehder. <BR> <BR>Lehder reports on the internet have surfaced naming him as the US man &#40;working for the CIA&#41; in charge of coke imports into the US, Lehder never spent a day in jail, and Lehder&#39;s wife was a former high ranking official at AIG Insurance in San Francisco. In fact in one report a journalist claims that Lehder&#39;s home phone number was LISTED in the Bay Area 411 directory in Lafayette a SF suburb.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13056-->
<!--Post: 13057--><!--Time: 1114040269-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13057"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 20, 2005 - 4:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Em <BR> <BR>I highly doubt that a Puerto Rican newspaper would have documented anything about our &#34;boys&#34; if the US govt was involved.  .  .  just a hunch but I think that is a dead end.  .  .  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13057-->
<!--Post: 13250--><!--Time: 1114655408-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13250"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, April 27, 2005 - 7:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->TAC, THIS CAME IN THE MAIL FROM OUR NEW FRIEND. <BR> <BR> <BR>I have a theory of my own to run by you about DR. I read some of the folks that think he started his homicide career  in Okinawa or Japan.  My own very strong feeling is that he killed for the first time in the Philippines. He could much more easily have gotten away with it while on Luzon than either on Oki or Honshu I think. The Philippine Islands are much more like the Wild Wild East. Would certainly like to see if his squadron did work at Clark AFB or satellite installations or whether he went TDY to the PI. Also, he may have taken leave and gone to the Philippines on his own or may even have caught some of the daily liaison flights between Kadena and Clark. I know that Futenma MAS to Subic Bay is just  a ---loud and uncomfortable---four hour trip in a C-130. A C141 between Kadena and Clark would be about two and a half hours one way.    <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13250-->
<!--Post: 13287--><!--Time: 1114809886-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13287"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tac<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tac<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 2:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Em <BR> <BR>Are you considering a Marcos connection ? <BR> <BR>The rumor mill has always churned heavy in Northern California re: Marcos and his possible role as a cocaine smuggler. I have nothing but rumor and inuendo to go on.  .  .   <BR> <BR>Our new friend ?  I have one guess. <BR> <BR>I find it rather interesting that in Phx first email he offered to &#34;pass on any more questions.&#34; <BR> <BR>My question is to whom is he passing on our questions ? If I am missing something here please <BR>enlighten me. <BR> <BR>Frankly the PRico connection seems to be the most solid if compared to a Rader scenario in the Phillipines.  .  .   <BR> <BR> <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 13287-->
<!--Post: 13292--><!--Time: 1114819474-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST13292"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, April 29, 2005 - 5:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No Tac, this one is in Texas and Very interested in the case and Ex-Military. Can&#39;t post. Just trying to help. I posted his ideas to see if it could help. Your friend Sheila<!--/Text--></td></tr>
